%%{init: {"sequence": {"wrapPadding": 18}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  participant P as Platform API (Next.js)
  participant DDB as DynamoDB
  participant SM as Secrets Manager
  participant GL as AWS Glue
  participant DATA as S3 Tables / Redshift
  participant OM as OpenMetadata
  U->>P: POST /api/sync/[id]/start
  P->>DDB: read sync task + data source
  Note over U,GL: This figure shows batch sync (Glue)<br/>Real-time CDC goes through /api/sync/[id]/start-realtime (DMS / Zero-ETL / Flink), see also deepdive-sync-flow
  P->>DATA: ensure S3 table bucket + namespace
  Note over P,GL: Full load: extract the whole table and rebuild it with overwrite<br/>Incremental: read only rows with incCol above the watermark, then append
  P->>GL: CreateJob + StartJobRun (Iceberg)
  P->>DDB: write run record (running)
  P-->>U: 200 {jobRunId, runId}
  par Glue job (asynchronous)
    GL->>SM: fetch source DB credentials
    GL->>DATA: extract from source → write S3 Tables / Redshift
    P->>GL: poll status → update run record
  and metadata push (fire-and-forget)
    P->>SM: fetch ingestion-bot JWT
    P->>OM: upsert source / S3 Tables / Redshift tables
    P->>OM: PUT lineage (source → S3 → Redshift, column level)
  end
